-- injection
refused  subject with a newline: mail.compose: subject contains a line break, which would let it write its own headers; remove it -- headers cannot span lines
ACCEPTED subject without one (the control)
refused  recipient with a newline: mail.compose: to contains a line break, which would let it write its own headers; remove it -- headers cannot span lines
refused  from with a CRLF: mail.compose: from contains a line break, which would let it write its own headers; remove it -- headers cannot span lines
refused  header value with a CRLF: mail.compose: header X-Note contains a line break, which would let it write its own headers; remove it -- headers cannot span lines
ACCEPTED header value without one (the control)
refused  attachment name with a newline: mail.compose: attachment name contains a line break, which would let it write its own headers; remove it -- headers cannot span lines
-- headers
refused  header name with a space: mail.compose: 'X Note' is not a valid header name -- letters, digits and '-' only
refused  a header mail.compose writes itself: mail.compose: 'Subject' is written by mail.compose; supplying it would put the field in the message twice
-- addresses
refused  no from: mail.compose: from is required
refused  no recipients: mail.compose: no recipients (to, cc and bcc are all empty)
refused  an address with no @: mail.compose: to is not an address (no '@'): nobody
refused  a space inside the address: mail.compose: to has a space inside the address: b b@example.com
refused  an unclosed angle bracket: mail.compose: to has '<' without a closing '>': Bee <b@example.com
ACCEPTED a closed one (the control)
-- shape
refused  a misspelled field: mail.compose: unknown field 'bodyy'; expected one of from, to, cc, bcc, reply_to, subject, body, html, attachments, headers, date
refused  an attachment with no content: mail.compose: each attachment needs a name and content
ACCEPTED an attachment with one (the control)
